<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Bio — Andreas Andreou</title><meta name="description" content="The story behind Andreas Andreou's work across law, public life and institution-building."><link rel="icon" href="assets/favicon.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header wrap"><a class="wordmark" href="/">Andreas Andreou</a><nav class="nav"><a href="/bio">Bio</a><a href="/work">Work</a><a href="/public-contribution">Public life</a><a href="https://www.procura.gr/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Procura ↗</a><a href="/#ideas">Ideas</a></nav><a class="contact" href="/#contact">Contact</a></header><main><section class="story-hero wrap"><img src="assets/arsakeio-graduation-2016.jpeg" alt="Andreas Andreou delivering a graduation address in 2016"><div class="story-copy"><span class="eyebrow">A personal story about choosing again</span><h1>The future looked certain. It just wasn’t mine.</h1><p class="lede">From medicine to law, from research to practice, and from advising institutions to serving inside one: the path has been a series of honest choices.</p></div></section><section class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Before the timeline</span><h2>The decisions between the milestones matter most.</h2><p>At eighteen, I was preparing to study medicine. After one year, I left for law — first in Nicosia, then at the University of Cyprus. Law became a way to understand systems and intervene in them, not simply a profession.</p><p>That instinct led through technology and data-security research in Brussels, commercial legal practice in Athens, and public service in Galatsi. Each environment made the next question sharper: how do rules, markets and institutions become outcomes people can actually feel?</p><div class="timeline"><span class="eyebrow">2016—2021</span><div><h3>Choosing law, then learning to communicate it.</h3><p>University of Cyprus · Rhetoric Club · Dikaio-logies radio programme.</p></div></div><div class="timeline"><span class="eyebrow">2022—2024</span><div><h3>Moving closer to where decisions become real.</h3><p>Cyber and data-security research in Brussels, followed by commercial practice and a campaign built from the ground up in Galatsi.</p></div></div><div class="timeline"><span class="eyebrow">2024—Now</span><div><h3>Inside the institution, and building beyond it.</h3><p>Municipal councillor and former deputy mayor; elected 10th among 400+ candidates and the youngest individual elected; founder of Procura; legal and regulatory work across Greece and Cyprus.</p></div></div></section><section class="section band"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">The work now</span><h2>Still choosing the work, not the title.</h2><a class="button" href="/#contact">Start a conversation ↗</a></div></section></main><footer class="footer wrap"><div><strong>Andreas Andreou</strong><small>Athens, Greece</small></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="mailto:andreoulegal@gmail.com">Email</a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andreoulegal" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><span>© 2026 Andreas Andreou</span><a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a></div></footer></body></html>
